<section class="phero"><div class="phero-bg"><img src="/assets/img/photos/handshake.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/handshake-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/handshake.webp 1200w" sizes="100vw" width="1200" height="799" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"></div><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><i aria-hidden="true">/</i><a href="/claim-planning-tools/">Claim tools</a><i aria-hidden="true">/</i><span aria-current="page">Claim File Strength Test</span></nav><p class="kicker">Free checklist</p><h1>Claim File Strength Test: Is Your File Appraisal-Ready?</h1><p class="lede">The strongest appraisals are won with the file you bring to the table. Answer twelve questions to see where yours stands and what to fix before anyone signs a demand.</p></div></section>
<section class="sec tool-sec"><div class="wrap"><div class="rv">
<div class="tool tool-wide" data-tool="ready">
  <div class="tool-head"><span>Claim file strength test</span><i>12 questions · about two minutes</i></div>
  <div class="tool-body">
    <div class="tool-in">
      <ol class="quiz"><li data-w="3" data-fix="Get written confirmation that coverage is accepted. If the claim was denied, talk to a North Dakota attorney before thinking about appraisal."><span>Has the insurer accepted coverage for at least part of the loss?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="3" data-fix="Ask in writing for the full line-item estimate, including the price list date."><span>Do you have the carrier’s complete, itemized estimate — not just a summary page?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="3" data-fix="Get an independent line-item estimate; a one-line lump-sum bid rarely holds up in front of a panel."><span>Do you have your own itemized estimate from a contractor or estimator?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Collect every photo with its date, and add current photos of the same areas."><span>Do you have dated photos taken soon after the storm or event?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Find the ‘Appraisal’ condition, note any deadlines and who pays what."><span>Have you read the appraisal paragraph in your policy’s conditions?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Locate the ‘Suit Against Us’ condition and put the date in a calendar — the policy clock planner can help."><span>Do you know your policy’s suit-limitation date?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Make reasonable temporary repairs (tarps, heat, water extraction) and keep every receipt."><span>Were temporary repairs made, with receipts saved?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Schedule a follow-up inspection once roofs and siding are clear so the scope is complete."><span>If the loss happened in winter, has snow-covered or frozen damage been re-inspected after thaw?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="1" data-fix="Download or request the declarations page that was in force on the date of loss."><span>Do you have your current declarations page?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Make sure concealed areas were inspected so the scope isn’t missing whole rooms or layers."><span>Is hidden damage (attic, decking, wet walls, basement) opened up and documented?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="1" data-fix="Gather letters, emails and adjuster notes into one dated file."><span>Is your correspondence with the carrier organized by date?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Run the award break-even calculator — a narrow gap may not justify appraisal costs."><span>Is the gap between estimates more than roughly 10% or several thousand dollars?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li>
      </ol>
      <div class="btn-row"><button type="button" class="btn ghost small" data-reset>Reset answers</button></div>
    </div>
    <div class="tool-out out-gauge" aria-live="polite">
      <div>
        <svg class="gauge" viewBox="0 0 200 110" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 100 A80 80 0 0 1 180 100" fill="none" stroke="#e3e9f7" stroke-width="18"/><path data-o="arc" d="M20 100 A80 80 0 0 1 180 100" fill="none" stroke="#ffd12b" stroke-width="18" stroke-dasharray="251.3" stroke-dashoffset="251.3" style="transition:stroke-dashoffset .5s,stroke .3s"/></svg>
        <div class="gauge-num"><span data-o="score">–</span></div>
        <p class="hint center">Answered <span data-o="count">0 / 12</span></p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="out-msg" data-o="verdict"></p>
        <p class="todo-h">Your to-do list</p>
        <ul class="todo" data-o="todo"></ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div></div>
<p class="hint center">For planning only. Results depend on the figures you enter and your policy’s terms; they aren’t a quote, an appraisal or legal advice.</p></div></section>
<div class="wrap layout"><article class="prose">
<h2>How the questions are weighted</h2>
<p>Coverage, estimates and evidence carry the most weight because they decide whether appraisal is even the right tool and how well your number will hold up. Administrative items matter too, but they’re quicker to fix. One question is specific to cold-weather losses: snow and ice can hide damage that only shows after thaw.</p>
<h2>What to do with your score</h2>
<ul><li><strong>75 and up:</strong> your file looks solid. A professional review of the gap is the logical next step.</li>
<li><strong>45 to 74:</strong> close the open items first; each one strengthens your position.</li>
<li><strong>Below 45:</strong> invoking appraisal now could lock in a low number. Build the file before you demand.</li></ul>

<h2>Questions about this tool</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Is anything I enter saved?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>No. The check runs entirely in your browser; nothing is stored or sent.</p></div></details><details><summary>Can I share the result?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Yes. Take a screenshot of the score and to-do list and bring it to a consultation.</p></div></details></div>
